==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{ety|ru|:inh|orv:учити<ety:inh<sla-pro:*učiti>>|tree=1}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|учити}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*učiti}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|учи́ть}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-учить.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|учи́ть|impf|pf=вы́учить,научи́ть,обучи́ть|vn=учёба<q:nomen actionis>,уче́ние<q:nomen actionis, nomen resultatis, nomen obiecti>,учи́тель<q:nomen agentis>,учени́к<q:nomen patientis>,учи́лище<q:nomen loci>,уче́бник<q:nomen instrumenti>}}

# to [[teach]], to [[instruct]] {{q|often not in an academic setting}} {{+obj|ru|acc<someone> + dat<a skill, principle, etc.>/inf<to do something>|&intransitive<qq:to be a teacher>}}
#: {{pf|ru|научи́ть|обучи́ть}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[она|Она́]] '''у́чит''' [[меня́]] [[англи́йскому]] [[языку́]].|She '''teaches''' me English.}}
#* {{RQ:Russian Synodal Bible|Mark|4|1|И опять начал '''учить''' при море; и собралось к Нему множество народа, так что Он вошел в лодку и сидел на море, а весь народ был на земле, у моря.|t=Again Jesus began to '''teach''' by the lake. The crowd that gathered round him was so large that He got into a boat and sat in it out on the lake, while all the people were along the shore at the water's edge.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to [[learn]], to [[study]] {{+obj|ru|acc<something> + :по(dat)<using a book or method>}}
#: {{pf|ru|вы́учить}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to [[memorize]] by rote
#: {{pf|ru|вы́учить}}
#: {{coi|ru|'''учи́ть''' [[роль]]|to '''memorize''' one's lines}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial|dated}} to [[beat]], to [[whip]] {{q|of [[corporal punishment]], often towards a child}} {{+obj|ru|acc<someone> + ins<with or using something>}}
#: {{coi|ru|'''учи́ть''' [[ремень|ремнём]]|to belt}}

